onduct issue attaches. The excess (36.34%) is below the 50% / 8.0 km materiality lines and your driver_profile shows 0 deviation flags over 553 completed 90-day trips, so there is no POL-RD-06 uplift and no conduct referral. Every gantry line is matched to the trace, so POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity does not fire and there is no phantom line. Your meter lines on distance and time are left untouched.\n\nRIDER: the answer to your question is that you should not be paying for gantries you never chose to cross. You are refunded the full $4.00 of CTE ERP; the rest of the fare — including the extra distance the closure forced — stands. The rider's contention that the detour was not rider-requested is accepted: the only CTE proposal came from the driver, your 'ok' is a bare acknowledgement, and waypoint_hint is null, so POL-RD-04 cannot be run and POL-RD-09(3) does not bar the ERP refund. The driver's contention that the diversion is fully excused under POL-RD-03 and that the ERP is the ceiling on recovery is also accepted.\n\nRULING: PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 4.00."
